# 1. TRUE PWM (Using standard edge-aligned w16)
# CZ Mode 1 (Saw->Pulse) pushes the 0.5 midpoint left and right.
# Because w16 jumps at 0.5, this perfectly widens and narrows the pulse!
v0 w16 a 5
c 1, 0         # CZ Mode 1 (Saw->Pulse), base distortion 0
cd 0.9         # Envelope sweeps distortion up to 90%
( 0.01 0.0  2.0 1.0  2.0 0.0 ) cte  # Slow PWM sweep envelope

# 2. PHASE SHIFT FLANGER (Using centered w49)
# Because w49 is centered, CZ Mode 1 pushes the entire pulse left and right
# without changing its width! Mixed with a static copy, it creates a flanger!
v1 w49 a 2
c 1, 0
cd 0.9
( 0.01 0.0  2.0 1.0  2.0 0.0 ) cte  # Slides the pulse phase forward and back

v2 w49 a 2     # Static copy to mix against v1
G 1 H 1        # Link to v1 so they trigger together
